    "retrieved": "2026-10-08",
    "evidence": "documented-adapted",
    "note": "Shape from the Atlassian response example: an array of IssueTypeWithStatus ({id, name, self, statuses[], subtask}), each status a StatusDetails ({description, iconUrl, id, name, self}). The published example omits statusCategory; StatusDetails documents it as a StatusCategory ({colorName, id, key, name, self}), so every status here carries one except \"Waiting for input\", which reproduces the omission. The keys new/indeterminate/done are the three research/15 J1a records as observed (backlog 535); the vendor documents no enum. Content is this repository's scenario with invented, neutral status names (BD-031): two issue types that share \"To pick up\", \"Doing\" and \"Done\", which the union by name (WP-172 ruling (a)) collapses."
  },
